 ## Current maintenance boundaries
 
 The maintained default sampling profile is Chair HYBRID START (`chair-hybrid`), the retained OT_HYBRID pilot1000 / conditional_total5000 endpoint. It requires explicit total N128..256; see `native_t1/docs/chair_start.md`. Historical N112 FM/JEdge5 sampling remains explicitly selectable; the old N112 trainer is not a START continuation trainer. MOMENT V2 and its finite-surface precursor activity packages and formal V2 weights are retired; preserved evidence and source archive are under `native_t1/maintenance/moment_retirement_20261005/` and the historical runs. Pair remains retired under `native_t1/maintenance/pair_cleanup_20261002_100559/`. Do not restore retired weights or start experiments merely to test scheduling. Official data/weights and retained checkpoints are protected. The 2026-10-05 START rollback and local Git commit were explicitly requested by the user; future commits/pushes still require user authorization.
+
+## Persistent research history: check prior routes before new experiments
+
+Before proposing or starting another Chair Control mechanism experiment, read [the research route memory](r2/docs/research_route_memory.md) and its [searchable route register](r2/docs/research_route_registry.json). The 2026-10-14 review groups 28 tested candidates without a stable upgrade and two pre-training gate blocks; these are mechanism families, not a claim that every approach is universally invalid. Source reports and hashes are indexed alongside the memory.
+
+Identify the closest prior route, its actual evidence boundary, the substantive change now proposed, and the observation that would justify the new test. This includes boundary/partner losses, context readout, B schedules, CAPPED/gradient limits, solver changes and denoiser iterations. Do not rename an old experiment or treat an old suggestion as unexecuted without checking its follow-up. This check should reuse existing evidence, not require another large audit or extra unbudgeted tests.
+
+Keep confirmed engineering fixes and bounded positive results separate from unsuccessful candidates. FULL_S6000 is the current sufficient-training method-comparison reference; CONTOUR_S6000 did not expand endpoint joint-success coverage. Neither result automatically changes the maintained CLI default. Preserve open-ended generation evaluation, regular coherent USER inputs (prefer K>=2), RAW/POST separation and original records. Retired checkpoint paths are historical; do not restore deleted weights or resume old jobs automatically. This memory does not authorize training, generation, cleanup, commit or push.--- WORKSPACE.md.before
